{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1744223,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"Aerostrike","festival_id":504454,"organization_id":675999,"web_url":"www.techfest26.com\/package","start_date":"2026-09-03T13:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-16T16:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/aerostrike-techfest26-annual-technical-festival-of-sliet-sant-longowal-institute-of-engineering-and-technol-1744223","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>AEROSTRIKE: Paper Plane Design Challenge:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Introduction:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>AEROSTRIKE is a test of aerodynamic design using paper.<\/li>\n<li>The challenge allows participants to conceptualize, craft, and launch paper aircraft that excel in flight distance, pinpoint accuracy, and structural stability.<\/li>\n<li>Participants can apply theoretical physics through a hands-on engineering challenge.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to all Diploma, UG, and PG students from any branch or discipline from recognized colleges or universities.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must carry a valid college ID card during the event for verification.<\/li>\n<li>Failure to produce a valid college ID may lead to disqualification.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Gameplay And Event Structure:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The challenge consists of a timed construction phase followed by two competitive rounds.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Construction Phase:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams will be provided with standard sheets of paper.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must construct their aircraft within 20 minutes.<\/li>\n<li>No extra time will be allotted after the construction phase ends.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 1: The Flight Test:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams will be called to the designated launch area one by one.<\/li>\n<li>Each team will make three hand-launched attempts to achieve maximum flight distance through gliding.<\/li>\n<li>The judges will record the best performance out of the three attempts for the final flight score.<\/li>\n<li>The top 5 teams will be selected for the Viva round.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Technical Viva:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team will participate in a 5-minute viva following the flight test.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must explain the aerodynamic principles and specific design choices behind their aircraft.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Scoring:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Distance Travelled: 30 Points.<\/li>\n<li>Aerodynamic Stability: 25 Points.<\/li>\n<li>Design Creativity and Stability: 20 Points.<\/li>\n<li>Discipline and Behaviour with Team: 10 Points.<\/li>\n<li>Viva: 15 Points.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Regulations:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Team size: Maximum of 3 participants per team.<\/li>\n<li>Only standard sheets of paper provided by the organizers at the venue are allowed.<\/li>\n<li>Participants may bring their own scissors and adhesive for construction purposes.<\/li>\n<li>Pre-folded planes, outside paper, or hidden weights are strictly prohibited and may result in immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>All folding must be done manually by the team members.<\/li>\n<li>Cutting and use of adhesives are allowed.<\/li>\n<li>Each aircraft must be launched entirely by hand from behind the designated launch line.<\/li>\n<li>Throwing aids and rubber bands are strictly prohibited.<\/li>\n<li>Stepping over or crossing the launch line during a throw will be considered a foul, and the attempt will not be scored.<\/li>\n<li>Teams may make minor aerodynamic adjustments, such as tweaking wing flaps, between their three attempts.<\/li>\n<li>Teams cannot construct a completely new aircraft once the flight round begins.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Flight Distance.<\/li>\n<li>Target Accuracy.<\/li>\n<li>Aerodynamic Stability.<\/li>\n<li>Creativity &amp; Design Innovation.<\/li>\n<li>Technical Knowledge (Viva).<\/li>\n<li>Discipline &amp; Conduct.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rewards &amp; Recognition:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Exciting prizes for the Top 3 Winners.<\/li>\n<li>Certificates for all participants.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Certification Policy:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All participants will receive certificates.<\/li>\n<li>Winners will be awarded certificates and prizes based on the final results declared by the judges.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Important Note:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Judges' decisions will be final and binding.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must bring a valid student ID and confirmation receipt.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must report 15 minutes before the event starts.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must respect the materials and venue rules.<\/li>\n<li>Any misconduct may lead to disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>The organizers reserve the right to modify the rules, schedule, or any aspect of the event with prior notice, in the best interest of the competition.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must stay updated through official notices on the SLIET techFEST 2026 website.<\/li>\n<li>Further modifications to the problem statement may be made based on subsequent analysis and requirements.<\/li>\n<li>Official Website: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\" data-rich-text-autolink=\"\">https:\/\/www.techfest26.com<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Accommodation and Meals:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Registration for the techFEST&rsquo;26 package is compulsory for accommodation and other perks, while participation in individual events is free*.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>For Further Query:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Domain Advisor: Raju Kumar, 2341023\/GCS, 6209681064.<\/li>\n<li>Domain Coordinator: Aisha Kumari, 2442003\/GCT, 6209681064.<\/li>\n<li>Event Coordinator: Himanshu Kumar, 254014015\/GCT, 8340358481.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":"","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":null,"registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27463276,"moderatio